config ZRAM_EXT
	tristate "Compressed RAM block device with writeback (zram_ext)"
	depends on ZRAM && m
	select ZSMALLOC
	help
	  A copy of the zram driver, built as the zram_ext module with
	  writeback to a backing device and per-slot access time tracking
	  always enabled. GKI builds zram.ko without CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK
	  and CONFIG_ZRAM_MEMORY_TRACKING, and a vendor module cannot change
	  that, so devices that need them load zram_ext.ko instead of
	  zram.ko. Both register the same block device and the same
	  zram-control class: only one of them can be loaded.

	  The default compressor is the one chosen for ZRAM.

	  See Documentation/admin-guide/blockdev/zram.rst for the interface.
